# After a Codex reply that edited files, one "Changed N files" row in the
# timeline opens that reply's files and their diffs (a sheet on a phone, the
# pane beside the chat on a wide screen). It counts the whole-turn diff,
# including a page the agent wrote from the shell that no edit row shows
# (+5 −1 across 2 files, where the rows alone say 1 file, +12 −4).
launch --fixture read-preview --fixture send-preview --fixture activity-preview --fixture response-turn-diff-preview
reveal down --id "reply-changes:turn"
wait --label "Changed 2 files, 5 added lines, 1 removed lines"
shot reply-changes-row
tap --id "reply-changes:turn"
wait --id reply-changes
wait --label "Sources/ChatView.swift, Swift, 2 added lines, 1 removed lines"
tap --id "reply-file:comic/index.html"
wait --contains "<title>Comic</title>"
shot edited-files-turn-diff
